From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mckenna654 <mckenna654@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 09:27:23 +1100
Subject: fix: the arrow goes round people where they stand now, not where they
 started

A trainer who wanders stops for good where they were beaten (the game changes
their movement type but not their saved position). The path kept the starting
tile blocked and the real one open, so the arrow walked into them; with Surf it
then led into the water and straight back out, for ever. Found by the whole-game
run on Route 13.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CNqSDphYuD2Aqe9TExdQMP

diff --git a/src/little_trainers_nav.c b/src/little_trainers_nav.c
index 0b87ce76b..57e854397 100644
--- a/src/little_trainers_nav.c
+++ b/src/little_trainers_nav.c
@@ -577,6 +577,7 @@ static void BlockStandingObjects(void)
 {
     const struct MapEvents *events = gMapHeader.events;
     u8 i;
+    u8 objectEventId;
 
     if (events != NULL)
     {
@@ -597,7 +598,13 @@ static void BlockStandingObjects(void)
             {
                 continue;
             }
-            BlockTile(template->x + MAP_OFFSET, template->y + MAP_OFFSET);
+            // Where they are now, if the game has them on the map: a trainer who wanders stops
+            // for good where they were beaten, which is not where they started.
+            objectEventId = GetObjectEventIdByLocalIdAndMap(template->localId, gSaveBlock1Ptr->location.mapNum, gSaveBlock1Ptr->location.mapGroup);
+            if (objectEventId < OBJECT_EVENTS_COUNT)
+                BlockTile(gObjectEvents[objectEventId].currentCoords.x, gObjectEvents[objectEventId].currentCoords.y);
+            else
+                BlockTile(template->x + MAP_OFFSET, template->y + MAP_OFFSET);
         }
     }
 
